  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I worked it out by hand, and running the function gives the same number.\n\nIt calls two modules:\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**\n\n`decoy_tax.py` and `decoy_shipping.py` aren't imported, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
